{"hash": "fbfbd2ed94d1794f", "text": "The clerk keeps nothing, so every memory is paper put back on the desk. There are five ways it comes back. One: the conversation itself. The app re-sends every message, every turn. Two: a memory the assistant keeps about you, a profile it writes itself. Claude, ChatGPT and Gemini all have one, and on Claude it's no longer a paid extra. Three: searching old chats with a tool. You'll see a line like: searched past chats. Four: stores outside the app, reached by tool calls. Memory files on your computer, which Claude Code keeps, or a page in Notion or Google Drive, through a connector. Five: rag, short for retrieval augmented generation, the general name for what three and four do. Fetch the relevant pieces, put them on the desk, then answer. Vector search is one way to fetch; coding agents now mostly search with plain file tools. Each one costs a tool call, desk space, or both. Memory and rag get their own lessons in The Code.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "c", "l", "e", "r", "k", " ", "k", "e", "e", "p", "s", " ", "n", "o", "t", "h", "i", "n", "g", ",", " ", "s", "o", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "m", "e", "m", "o", "r", "y", " ", "i", "s", " ", "p", "a", "p", "e", "r", " ", "p", "u", "t", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", " ", "o", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "d", "e", "s", "k", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "a", "r", "e", " ", "f", "i", "v", "e", " ", "w", "a", "y", "s", " ", "i", "t", " ", "c", "o", "m", "e", "s", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", ".", " ", "O", "n", "e", ":", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "o", "n", "v", "e", "r", "s", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n", " ", "i", "t", "s", "e", "l", "f", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "a", "p", "p", " ", "r", "e", "-", "s", "e", "n", "d", "s", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "m", "e", "s", "s", "a", "g", "e", ",", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "t", "u", "r", "n", ".", " ", "T", "w", "o", ":", " ", "a", " ", "m", "e", "m", "o", "r", "y", " ", "t", "h", "e", " 